(BRANDGUARD OFFICIAL MARKETING & BRAND GOVERNANCE POLICIES \(2026\)) '
T*
(Section 1: General Tone and Verification Directives) '
(RULE 4: Marketing content must use professional and respectful language.) '
(All campaign copy, customer communications, and public advertisements must maintain an authoritative, dignified, and courteous tone. Emotional manipulation and deceptive hype are strictly forbidden.) '
T*
(RULE 5: Product benefits must be supported by approved information.) '
(Every statement asserting technical capabilities, operational speed, or efficacy must be backed by documented evidence approved by the product engineering council.) '
T*
(Section 2: Outcome Prohibitions and Superiority Restrictions) '
(RULE 1: Marketing content must not promise guaranteed results.) '
(Organizations and marketing authors must never assure universal outcomes or infallible success. Performance fluctuates based on customer operational environments.) '
T*
(RULE 2: Absolute performance claims such as "100% guaranteed" are prohibited.) '
(Phrases including '100% guaranteed', 'guarantees 100% results', 'never fails', and 'risk-free' are strictly prohibited in marketing and sales materials.) '
T*
(RULE 3: Unverified claims that a product is the best in the world are prohibited.) '
(Superlative market leadership assertions such as 'best solution in the world' or '#1 in the world' must be supported by verified, accredited third-party audited proof before public distribution.) '
T*
ET

